    "created_at": "2016-05-10T04:41:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-10T04:41:46Z",
    "body": "(Yes, `getDisplayMedia()`, I should know better.)\n\nThat actually makes me reconsider :)  Because of the inverse of your suggestion: screen capture is inherently very worrying and while we won't have persistent permission for screen capture, there is the risk that the framed site uses the good name of the top-level context to gain access to something it shouldn't.  I'm thinking that option 1 is no good now.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
